WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.407 --> 00:00:17.309
and his companions walked through the Western Paradise.

2
00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:22.491
The road weaved through a field of flowers and toward the Spirit Mountain.

3
00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:26.914
Bajie looked up at the huge mountain and shook his head.

4
00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:30.436
"It won't be easy to climb that."

5
00:00:31.732 --> 00:00:32.712
Wukong laughed.

6
00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:35.413
"Don't ask me to carry you!"

7
00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:41.135
The travelers soon arrived at a river with a strong current.

8
00:00:42.455 --> 00:00:46.897
Waves crashed into jagged rocks, spraying water everywhere.

9
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:50.898
"This river looks dangerous," said Wujing.

10
00:00:50.918 --> 00:00:54.439
"But we must cross it to get to the Spirit Mountain."

11
00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:57.240
Bajie sighed.

12
00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:01.687
"We will never be able to cross this river safely.

13
00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:03.808
Let's just go home."

14
00:01:03.828 --> 00:01:06.831
"Nonsense," said Wukong.

15
00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:09.553
"Look over there."

16
00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:12.455
The monkey pointed upstream.

17
00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:15.798
A thin log lay across the river.

18
00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:20.122
It wobbled and shook as the water rushed under it.

19
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.244
The Tang Monk looked at the log.

20
00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:25.286
"Don't be silly, Wukong.

21
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.908
We can't walk across that log—it's too thin.

22
00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:30.989
And it looks quite slippery."

23
00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:36.271
"But that log is the only way to reach the Spirit Mountain," said Wukong.

24
00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:39.373
"You must believe that it's safe.

25
00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:40.993
Watch me!"

26
00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:46.235
The monkey hopped onto the log and ran across the river and back.

27
00:01:53.418 --> 00:01:55.479
"See?" he said.

28
00:01:55.499 --> 00:01:57.020
"It's safe."

29
00:01:58.784 --> 00:01:59.824
Bajie snorted.

30
00:01:59.844 --> 00:02:02.745
"You don't weigh much, Wukong.

31
00:02:03.565 --> 00:02:05.886
But if I step on that log, it will break."

32
00:02:05.906 --> 00:02:09.467
"I believe Wukong," said Wujing.

33
00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:14.068
"We must walk across the log."

34
00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:16.289
"Follow me, Master," said Wukong.

35
00:02:17.469 --> 00:02:19.670
He pulled the Tang Monk toward the log.

36
00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.831
The monk trembled with fear.

37
00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:24.911
"Don't make me walk across that!

38
00:02:25.651 --> 00:02:27.352
I'll fall into the river and drown!"

39
00:02:28.524 --> 00:02:31.766
"Let's just fly over the river," suggested Bajie.

40
00:02:31.786 --> 00:02:34.668
"We can carry Master and the horse."

41
00:02:36.369 --> 00:02:37.930
"No," insisted Wukong.

42
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.872
"The Tang Monk must make the entire journey by himself.

43
00:02:42.932 --> 00:02:45.134
We're here to protect him, not to carry him.

44
00:02:46.354 --> 00:02:51.197
Buddha won't allow Master to have the True Scriptures if he doesn't take every step himself."

45
00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:55.760
Just then an old man appeared in a boat.

46
00:02:57.924 --> 00:03:00.466
"I can take you across the river," said the man.

47
00:03:00.486 --> 00:03:03.167
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

48
00:03:06.049 --> 00:03:07.309
He walked to the riverbank.

49
00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:13.433
"My companion wanted me to walk across that log, but—" The monk gasped.

50
00:03:13.453 --> 00:03:17.695
"There's something wrong with your boat," he said to the man.

51
00:03:17.715 --> 00:03:20.076
"It has no bottom!

52
00:03:21.217 --> 00:03:22.618
Water is flowing right through it!"

53
00:03:24.099 --> 00:03:26.060
"The boat is safe," said the man.

54
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.860
"Please climb in.

55
00:03:28.401 --> 00:03:29.381
Buddha is waiting."

56
00:03:30.481 --> 00:03:34.682
With a bit more hesitation, the Tang Monk stepped into the boat.

57
00:03:41.124 --> 00:03:44.085
He was shocked to find that he didn't sink.

58
00:03:45.106 --> 00:03:48.827
He sat on the edge of the boat as Wujing led the horse aboard.

59
00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:52.608
Bajie and Wukong followed.

60
00:03:57.728 --> 00:03:59.970
The boat glided swiftly across the river.

61
00:04:02.932 --> 00:04:04.513
Suddenly there was a splash.

62
00:04:07.415 --> 00:04:11.438
The Tang Monk looked at the water and saw a body floating downstream.

63
00:04:13.239 --> 00:04:13.980
He screamed.

64
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.481
"A man has drowned!"

65
00:04:16.602 --> 00:04:19.884
Wukong put his hand on the monk's shoulder and smiled.

66
00:04:19.904 --> 00:04:21.685
"It's you, Master."

67
00:04:21.705 --> 00:04:24.027
"What?" said the monk.

68
00:04:24.047 --> 00:04:27.161
"Me?" "Wukong is right!"

69
00:04:27.321 --> 00:04:28.142
cried Bajie.

70
00:04:28.162 --> 00:04:29.603
"It is you!"

71
00:04:29.623 --> 00:04:33.506
"Look again, Master," said Wujing, smiling.

72
00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.410
The Tang Monk looked at the body more carefully.

73
00:04:38.591 --> 00:04:41.813
It was wearing the same Buddhist robe that he was wearing.

74
00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:45.737
"It is me," said the monk quietly.

75
00:04:45.757 --> 00:04:51.642
"But how "You got rid of your mortal body, Master," said Wukong.

76
00:04:51.662 --> 00:04:54.024
"You're a spirit now."

77
00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.081
"You're one of us!"

78
00:04:56.521 --> 00:04:57.581
Bajie beamed.

79
00:05:04.045 --> 00:05:08.107
The boat soon reached the other riverbank, and the travelers stepped out.

80
00:05:17.032 --> 00:05:21.915
As they walked up the slope of the Spirit Mountain, the Tang Monk laughed in amazement.

81
00:05:24.756 --> 00:05:25.816
"I feel so light!"

82
00:05:26.077 --> 00:05:26.517
he said.

83
00:05:26.537 --> 00:05:29.298
"I feel like I could run right up this mountain!"

84
00:05:29.318 --> 00:05:31.979
"Good," said Bajie.

85
00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:34.060
"Perhaps you could carry me?"

86
00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.261
Everybody laughed as they continued up the mountain.
